usage: vera [-h] [--store STORE]
            {pour,remember,forget,ask,index,read-events,read,ledger,realize,observe,route,mcp-config,tool,documents,domain,doctor,stats,conduct,guard,heartbeat,propose-ai-facts,review-ai-facts,chat,math,simplify,code,compile,verify,hub,lab,mcp,field,lexicon,self-evolve,placement,sovereign,self-audit,audit,serve,setup,wizard,agent,obfuscate,deobfuscate,watermark,push-store}
            ...

vera — CLI for Verantyx Vera α (lab + chat in one binary).

Knowledge:
  vera pour --source synthetic|wikitext|hf:<name>[#config][:field]|file:<path>
  vera remember "The bright apple is sweet ."
  vera ask "what is apple"
  vera forget apple
  vera stats
  vera chat                    interactive REPL (knowledge + math + code)

Math / logic:
  vera math "x + 3 = 7"        wire arithmetic / typed equations
  vera simplify "x + 0"        term rewriting (rules are data)

Code reasoning:
  vera code ingest <path>
  vera code ask "who calls foo"

Lab:
  vera lab                     run the fork self-test suites
  vera mcp                     start the MCP server (see docs/MCP.md)

Conductor:
  vera conduct --frame F --repo R --adapter codex|claude|fake [--dry-run]
                               read a project frame and start (or plan) an agent
                               (see docs/CONDUCT_ENTRY.md); a frame with an [agents]
                               table is routed: omit --adapter (docs/AGENT_ROUTING.md)

Default store: ./vera_store.json (override with --store).

positional arguments:
  {pour,remember,forget,ask,index,read-events,read,ledger,realize,observe,route,mcp-config,tool,documents,domain,doctor,stats,conduct,guard,heartbeat,propose-ai-facts,review-ai-facts,chat,math,simplify,code,compile,verify,hub,lab,mcp,field,lexicon,self-evolve,placement,sovereign,self-audit,audit,serve,setup,wizard,agent,obfuscate,deobfuscate,watermark,push-store}
    pour                stream a corpus into the store
    remember            teach one sentence
    forget              delete a core (really deletes)
    ask                 one-shot question (typed verdict)
    index               does this already exist? one search over doors,
                        commands, modules, forks and every prereg/result —
                        derived, never listed
    read-events         read one sentence and return its event crosses
                        (predicate = centre, roles = arms, words = fillers) as
                        one line; same output as `python -m
                        verantyx.semantic_read --text=... --events`
    read                read one sentence (same output as `python -m
                        verantyx.semantic_read`); with --holes a sentence the
                        reader abstains on because of a filler's placement is
                        returned with its typed holes (docs/FUSION.md section
                        6)
    ledger              W10-f04: the testimony ledger of LLM candidates
                        (append-only, hash-chained): list | show <id> |
                        confirm <id> (a human confirms)
    realize             validate a cross-token line and realize one supported
                        event cross as a sentence
    observe             observe a structure from a viewpoint (anchor,
                        direction, range, ledger state) and realize what is
                        seen as one json line; every clause carries its
                        coordinate (docs/OBSERVATION.md)
    route               read a human's free-text explanation of the agents and
                        route one job (reading -> event cross -> relations ->
                        records -> router); one line out, 'undecided' (typed)
                        whenever any sentence could not be read
    mcp-config          print (or install) the MCP snippet pointing a client
                        at this binary and this store
    tool                call any of the MCP doors from the CLI (same doors,
                        second entrance — nothing is rewritten per command)
    documents           load documents into the store from the CLI — PDF,
                        Word, HTML, CSV, JSON, text; a directory is walked
    domain              register/inspect domain vocabularies
    doctor              self-check both faces on THIS machine: the covenant
                        guard (G1-G4) and the standalone device (S1-S4). Exit
                        1 if broken
    stats               store statistics
    conduct             read a project frame (.md or .jsonl) and start an
                        implementation agent; exit 0 ok/planned, 1 incomplete,
                        2 typed refusal, 3 internal error
    guard               covenant guard fast path: no federation load,
                        covenants.json only — for Claude Code hooks (stdin:
                        JSON payload)
    heartbeat           Milestone M: scan growth signals, draft+verify
                        candidate domain modules, queue for human review
                        (never auto-activates)
    propose-ai-facts    quarantine sentence candidates from an AI's FINAL text
                        (never thinking/chain-of-thought)
    review-ai-facts     review quarantined AI-proposed facts (arrow-key
                        accept/reject)
    chat                interactive REPL (lab | hybrid | round5)
    math                wire arithmetic / typed equations
    simplify            term rewriting (algebra rules)
    code                code reasoning: ingest / ask
    compile             read your documents into a checkable store (no
                        training)
    verify              check what an AI wrote against your compiled documents
    hub                 speak across centre edges (core to core), no model
    lab                 run fork self-test suites
    mcp                 start MCP server (stdio)
    field               the full local app for a municipal desk (127.0.0.1, no
                        network)
    lexicon             ask the configured static dictionary about a word
    self-evolve         prove defects from the documents themselves, repair,
                        and keep
    placement           simulate which facts go on the faces, before shipping
                        a store
    sovereign           build one federated node from documents, stage by
                        stage
    self-audit          find structural signals of defects, with no person
                        reading
    audit               drop documents in a browser and read what the engine
                        did
    serve               Milestone N: HTTP+SSE daemon (Vera as harness, not an
                        MCP tool) — POST /agent/run, GET /events?run_id=, GET
                        /agent/run/<id>
    setup               interactive settings (LLM, allocation)
    wizard              guided data-placement (arrow keys)
    agent               agent mode: tools + ReAct + approvals
    obfuscate           reversible identifier obfuscation, mapping encrypted
                        with a key derived from your store's personal state
    deobfuscate         restore original names
    watermark           leak attribution: register an owner's naming-variant,
                        or identify candidate owners of an obfuscated file
                        (evidence, not proof — see docs/WATERMARK.md)
    push-store          upload the store to HuggingFace

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --store STORE         store path (default: config, else vera_store.json)
